# Guiding Center 4d Small Tokamak Deeply Trapped with Gauss-Legendre Runge-Kutta Methods

The same orbit family as on the [medium-size tokamak](../guiding-center-4d-deeply-trapped/guiding-center-4d-deeply-trapped-firk-gauss.md),
in the small tokamak equilibrium in cylindrical coordinates. Its particles are far slower —
`u ~ 8 \cdot 10^{-4}` against the medium tokamak's `3 \cdot 10^{-1}` — so the orbit needs a time
step three hundred times larger, `\Delta t = 800`, which is the one the pre-0.2 gallery used for it.
Over the 12500 steps run here the orbit closes many hundreds of times.

The toroidal momentum is shown alongside the energy, as the second invariant of the guiding centre
dynamics; both are set in `src/guiding-center-4d.jl`.

```julia
run_list(odeproblem(), "Guiding Center 4d Small Tokamak Deeply Trapped", tableaus_firk_gauss())
```
